      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a good idea but I\u0027m not sure it makes sense in practice. OpenSSH still treats the key format for these keys as `ssh-rsa`, even when generating new ones with e.g. `ssh-keygen -t rsa-sha2-256`. Additionally, there\u0027s a lot of code that relies heavily on the public key type being `ssh-rsa`. I think it\u0027s a lot of work that would be better solved by changing the default host key algorithms.",
